{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MAXN = 5000010;\nconst int INF = 1000000000;\n\ninline int idx(int x, int k, int n) { return x + (k - 1) * n; }\n\ntemplate<typename T>\ninline void read(T &x) {\n    x = 0;\n    char c = getchar();\n    bool neg = false;\n    while (!isdigit(c)) { if (c == '-') neg = true; c = getchar(); }\n    while (isdigit(c)) { x = (x << 1) + (x << 3) + (c ^ 48); c = getchar(); }\n    if (neg) x = -x;\n}\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to, nxt, cap, cost;\n};\n\nint n, m, k, v1, v2, s, t;\nint dist[MAXN];\nbool inQueue[MAXN];\nEdge edges[MAXN];\nint head[MAXN], ecnt = 1;\n\nvoid addEdge(int u, int v, int cap, int cost) {\n    edges[++ecnt] = {v, head[u], cap, cost};\n    head[u] = ecnt;\n    edges[++ecnt] = {u, head[v], 0, -cost};\n    head[v] = ecnt;\n}\n\nbool spfa() {\n    queue<int> q;\n    fill(dist + s, dist + t + 1, INF);\n    fill(inQueue + s, inQueue + t + 1, false);\n    q.push(s);\n    dist[s] = 0;\n    inQueue[s] = true;\n\n    while (!q.empty()) {\n        int u = q.front();\n        q.pop();\n        inQueue[u] = false;\n\n        for (int i = head[u]; i; i = edges[i].nxt) {\n            int v = edges[i].to, c = edges[i].cost;\n            if (edges[i].cap > 0 && dist[v] > dist[u] + c) {\n                dist[v] = dist[u] + c;\n                if (!inQueue[v]) {\n                    inQueue[v] = true;\n                    q.push(v);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return dist[t] != INF;\n}\n\nint dfs(int u, int flowLimit, bool vis[]) {\n    if (u == t) return flowLimit;\n    vis[u] = true;\n    int pushed = 0, total = flowLimit;\n\n    for (int i = head[u]; i; i = edges[i].nxt) {\n        int v = edges[i].to, cap = edges[i].cap;\n        if (vis[v] || cap == 0 || dist[v] != dist[u] + edges[i].cost) continue;\n\n        int f = dfs(v, min(total, cap), vis);\n        if (f > 0) {\n            total -= f;\n            edges[i].cap -= f;\n            edges[i ^ 1].cap += f;\n            pushed += f;\n            if (total == 0) break;\n        }\n    }\n    return pushed;\n}\n\nint minCostMaxFlow() {\n    int totalFlow = 0, totalCost = 0;\n    while (spfa()) {\n        bool vis[MAXN] = {false};\n        int flow = dfs(s, INF, vis);\n        if (flow > 0) {\n            totalFlow += flow;\n            totalCost += flow * dist[t];\n        }\n    }\n    return totalCost;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    read(n), read(m), read(k), read(v1), read(v2);\n    t = idx(n, 110, n) + 1;\n\n    for (int i = 2; i <= 110; ++i)\n        addEdge(idx(1, i, n), t, INF, 0);\n\n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 1; j < 110; ++j)\n            addEdge(idx(i, j, n), idx(i, j + 1, n), INF, v1);\n\n    for (int i = 1, x; i <= k; ++i) {\n        read(x);\n        addEdge(s, idx(x, 1, n), 1, 0);\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= m; ++i) {\n        int x, y;\n        read(x), read(y);\n        for (int j = 1; j < 110; ++j)\n            for (int l = 1; l <= k; ++l) {\n                int cost = v2 * (2 * l - 1) + v1;\n                addEdge(idx(x, j, n), idx(y, j + 1, n), 1, cost);\n                addEdge(idx(y, j, n), idx(x, j + 1, n), 1, cost);\n            }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\", minCostMaxFlow());\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\nMAXN = 5000010\nINF = 1000000000\n\ndef idx(x, k, n):\n    return x + (k - 1) * n\n\ndef read_int():\n    line = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    if not line:\n        return None\n    return int(line)\n\nclass Edge:\n    __slots__ = ('to', 'nxt', 'cap', 'cost')\n    def __init__(self, to, nxt, cap, cost):\n        self.to = to\n        self.nxt = nxt\n        self.cap = cap\n        self.cost = cost\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    m = int(next(it))\n    k = int(next(it))\n    v1 = int(next(it))\n    v2 = int(next(it))\n    \n    t = idx(n, 110, n) + 1\n    \n    edges = []\n    head = [-1] * MAXN\n    ecnt = 1\n    \n    def add_edge(u, v, cap, cost):\n        nonlocal ecnt\n        edges.append(Edge(v, head[u], cap, cost))\n        head[u] = ecnt\n        ecnt += 1\n        edges.append(Edge(u, head[v], 0, -cost))\n        head[v] = ecnt\n        ecnt += 1\n    \n    for i in range(2, 111):\n        add_edge(idx(1, i, n), t, INF, 0)\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, 110):\n            add_edge(idx(i, j, n), idx(i, j + 1, n), INF, v1)\n    \n    s = 0\n    for i in range(k):\n        x = int(next(it))\n        add_edge(s, idx(x, 1, n), 1, 0)\n    \n    for i in range(m):\n        x = int(next(it))\n        y = int(next(it))\n        for j in range(1, 110):\n            for l in range(1, k + 1):\n                cost = v2 * (2 * l - 1) + v1\n                add_edge(idx(x, j, n), idx(y, j + 1, n), 1, cost)\n                add_edge(idx(y, j, n), idx(x, j + 1, n), 1, cost)\n    \n    dist = [INF] * MAXN\n    in_queue = [False] * MAXN\n    \n    def spfa():\n        for i in range(s, t + 1):\n            dist[i] = INF\n            in_queue[i] = False\n        \n        q = deque()\n        q.append(s)\n        dist[s] = 0\n        in_queue[s] = True\n        \n        while q:\n            u = q.popleft()\n            in_queue[u] = False\n            \n            i = head[u]\n            while i != -1:\n                edge = edges[i]\n                v = edge.to\n                c = edge.cost\n                if edge.cap > 0 and dist[v] > dist[u] + c:\n                    dist[v] = dist[u] + c\n                    if not in_queue[v]:\n                        in_queue[v] = True\n                        q.append(v)\n                i = edge.nxt\n        \n        return dist[t] != INF\n    \n    def dfs(u, flow_limit, vis):\n        if u == t:\n            return flow_limit\n        vis[u] = True\n        pushed = 0\n        total = flow_limit\n        \n        i = head[u]\n        while i != -1:\n            edge = edges[i]\n            v = edge.to\n            cap = edge.cap\n            if vis[v] or cap == 0 or dist[v] != dist[u] + edge.cost:\n                i = edge.nxt\n                continue\n            \n            f = dfs(v, min(total, cap), vis)\n            if f > 0:\n                total -= f\n                edges[i].cap -= f\n                edges[i ^ 1].cap += f\n                pushed += f\n                if total == 0:\n                    break\n            i = edge.nxt\n        \n        return pushed\n    \n    total_flow = 0\n    total_cost = 0\n    \n    while spfa():\n        vis = [False] * MAXN\n        flow = dfs(s, INF, vis)\n        if flow > 0:\n            total_flow += flow\n            total_cost += flow * dist[t]\n    \n    print(total_cost)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013374387344811112, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1